Install Docker

Now let's install Docker.

Command
sudo apt install docker.io -y

Before running, let's understand it.

sudo

Run as administrator.

apt

Ubuntu package manager.

install

Install software.

docker.io

Docker package name available in Ubuntu repositories.

-y

Automatically answer "yes" to installation prompts.

After Installation

Run these commands one by one:

sudo systemctl enable docker

What it does:

Makes Docker start automatically whenever the server boots.

sudo systemctl start docker

What it does:

Starts the Docker service immediately.

sudo systemctl status docker

What it does:

Checks whether Docker is running.

You should see:

active (running)
Verification

Run:

docker --version

Then:

sudo docker run hello-world

The hello-world image is Docker's test image.

What happens internally:

Docker Hub
      |
Downloads hello-world image
      |
Creates container
      |
Runs container
      |
Displays success message

This proves:

✅ Docker Engine is installed

✅ Docker can pull images

✅ Docker can create containers
